<title>VENEZUELA: CANTV workers to sell shares on international mkt.</title>
<headline>CANTV workers to sell shares on international mkt.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-05-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Employee shareholders of Venezuela's CANTV are planning an organised share sale on international markets, according to an advertisement taken out in the Venezuelan press on Sunday.</p>
<p>The sale involves class C shares which represent 10.85 percent of the company and can be held only by employees or retired employees of the privatised company.</p>
<p>Shareholder representatives working with the Fondo de Inversiones Venezolanos had chosen Lehman Bros and SBC Warburg to coordinate the operation, the advertisement said.</p>
<p>((-- Ana Isabel Martinez, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
